<title>UK: ScotAm shareholders agree Prudential merger.</title>
<headline>ScotAm shareholders agree Prudential merger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British mutually-owned insurance group Scottish Amicable said on Friday its shareholders had overwhelmingly approved the company's takeover by Prudential Corp Plc.</p>
<p>Scottish Amicable said shareholders at a special meeting cast 98 percent of their votes in favour of the deal, which will transfer its business to Prudential.</p>
<p>The transfer was seen taking effect on September 30.</p>
<p>Prudential beat out rivals Abbey National Plc and Australian Mutual Provident (AMP) in winning control of Scottish Amicable. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
